# World Data

The world is open and procedurally generated. Runtime world state splits into two layers:

## Base (immutable)

`RegionBase` holds generated, unchangeable data per region: height maps, biome flags, RNG seeds (`LCGs`). Stored as `RegionBase_x*_y*.bin` via `FileManager.GetRegionBaseFilePath`.

Base data is produced offline/at generation time (`Game.WorldGeneration`) and treated as read-only at runtime.

## Patches (mutable)

Player/world mutations are recorded as **patches**:

- `RegionChanges` — groups of patch files per region (`PatchesGroup_x*_y*.bin`)
- `ChunkPatch` — per-chunk command stream (create/delete entities, height edits, health, …)

Patches layer on top of base data. When loading a chunk, apply base + accumulated patches.

## Transfer Mechanism

World data transfer is **separate from EventsStream**:

- Local persistence: `FileManager`, `Storage`, async `FileIoTask` loads
- Remote/multiplayer: `ServerStorageDelegates`, `RemoteServer.GetChunkPatches`, `GetServerStorageDelegates`

Do not send terrain or chunk patch payloads through EventsStream.

## Access Patterns

- `Storage` (native, Burst-friendly) — access from `ThreadRules.MainJob` only
- `Storage.Managed` — disk I/O orchestration from `ThreadRules.SyncPhase`
- Chunk lifecycle callbacks via `IChunkProcessor.ChunkLoadedOrUpdated` / `RegionBaseLoaded`

When adding world mutations, append to patch command streams (`ChunkPatch` command types), not to `RegionBase`. For chunk versioning, sync, and patch mutation rules, see `world-chunks`.
